    {
        "tag": "playsound",
        "key": "$d_avg_tinnitus",
        "volume": 1
    },
    {
        "text": "Hautin has wondered many times before: If she were actually in the middle of a Catastrophe, what would she hear?"
    },
    {
        "text": "The howling of the wind? The roaring of explosions? The shrieking of the panicked crowd? Turns out it is none of those."
    },
    {
        "text": "It is the sound of walls and metal structures being squashed as flat as an empty can, one after the other."
    },
    {
        "text": "It is a sound that instills extreme terror in oh-so-fragile humans, who begin to worry their organs, bones, and blood vessels will suffer a similar fate."
    },
    {
        "tag": "dialog"
    },
